Slave to no Sect, who takes no private road,
But looks thro' Nature up to Nature's God,
Purfues that Chain which links th' immense Design,
Joyns Heav'n, and Earth, and mortal, and divine;
Sees, that no Being any Blifs can know 330
But touches some above, and some below;
Learns, from this Union of the rising Whole,
The first, last Purpose of the human Soul;
And knows, where Faith, Law, Morals all began,
All end, in Love of God, and Love of Man. 335

